From 8bfe7b344589072cea4387bfd3b596c62afd047c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rafe Walker <45343084+rafe-walker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 13:59:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 05/17] feat(mcp): list feature flags with a rollout summary

"List flags with their rollout" took 4 calls and 11,229 tokens on the
friction session (A15): feature-flag-get-all rows carried no rollout,
the instructions sent the question to SQL (info execute-sql alone was
10,742 tokens), and system.feature_flags has neither `active` nor
`tags`, so the tag filter still needed the list tool.

feature-flag-get-all rows already carry `active` and `tags`. They now
also carry `rollout`, a one-line summary of the release conditions and
variants, for example

    75% where $browser = Chrome; 100% where friction-plan = pro | variants: control 50%, test 50%

The list response already has `filters`, so this is done in services/mcp
with no backend change: the include allowlist keeps the condition
fields the summary needs, and a new afterResponse hook
(featureFlags/listRolloutHooks) replaces them with the summary.
Payloads and every other filter field stay out of the row. Adding
`active` and `tags` columns to system.feature_flags would need a
backend change and is not done here.

The execute-sql guidance listed flags with
`SELECT key, name, rollout_percentage FROM system.feature_flags`, whose
top-level rollout_percentage is a legacy column that was null for both
flags (B8). The example now selects the release conditions from
`filters.groups`, says the top-level column is usually null, and points
at feature-flag-get-all for state, tags and rollout.

The tool description says what each row carries; the generated
definition JSON is edited to match, because codegen needs the backend
OpenAPI schema.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
